# Build context = repo root. The image bundles the SELF-CONTAINED engine:
# src/ (code + viewer/ assets + templates/ skeletons) and requirements.txt. The
# content (the "mind") arrives at runtime via git clone into /app/repo — NOT via
# the image. So everything else is excluded: a minimal context, and above all
# .git (whose .git/config may hold the GitHub PAT) kept out of the image.
*
!src
!requirements.txt
# The viewer's dev toolchain (its node_modules alone is ~80 MB) and sources stay out,
# like in the wheel (pyproject.toml exclude-package-data): the image needs only the
# built viewer.
src/viewer/build
src/viewer/tailwind
src/viewer/jsfmt
src/viewer/lib
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
